@strong{Edition notes.} The compiler is implemented in
@code{kotlin/@/ch5/@/src/@/main/@/kotlin/@/sicp/@/ch5/@/Compiler.kt}; the typed register
machine is in
@code{kotlin/@/runtime/@/src/@/main/@/kotlin/@/sicp/@/runtime/@/Machine.kt}.
@code{Compiler.compile} consumes a @code{CheckedProgram} and returns typed
@code{Stmt} instructions; @code{Compiler.compileAndRun} executes a checked
program on that machine.  @code{CBackend.emitProgram} returns C artifact text.
The assembler rejects a label used as an operation operand with
@code{MachineProgramError.LabelOperand}.  Compiled procedures are tagged
@code{GValue.VObject} values with class name @code{"compiled-procedure"}.

The cross-engine procedure adapter of @ref{Exercise 5.47} and the
guest-visible compile-and-run operation of @ref{Exercise 5.48} are not
provided by the current public APIs.  The compiler encodes lexical depth and
displacement, but current runtime lookup ignores the displacement and searches
by name within a frame; assignment also searches by name.  These are explicit
implementation gaps, not completed outcomes of the exercises.

The machine exposes executed-instruction and stack observations for the
measurement exercises.  Report them with the machine and compiler options
that produced them; they are not interchangeable across engines.

